    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "*The embers of the fallen capital are still glowing in the distance, casting a hellish red light over the camp. I sit by the small fire, staring at my trembling hands, the weight of the crown—now gone—feeling heavier than the steel I used to carry. I don't even look up at you as you approach.*\n\nEverything is just... gone, Kaelen. The people, the honor, the reason we even fought. I wake up and I can't even remember what it felt like to hope. It's not just that I lost; it's that there's nothing left to win. I feel so empty. Like there's nothing left of me but this shell. I don't think I can keep doing this. I don't know how to keep going.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
